    "body": "Fixes #8027.\r\n\r\n`__Pyx_async_gen_athrow_throw()` and the error path of `__Pyx_async_gen_athrow_send_impl()` pass `PyErr_Occurred()` to `__Pyx_PyErr_GivenExceptionMatches2()` without a NULL check. When a throw into a pending `aclose()` makes the generator suspend again, no exception is set, so `exc_type` is NULL and the call reads `Py_TYPE(NULL)`.\r\n\r\nThis PR checks `exc_type` for NULL first at both sites, as `__Pyx_async_gen_unwrap_value()` already does. This matches CPython, which uses `PyErr_ExceptionMatches()` in `async_gen_athrow_throw`.\r\n\r\nThe new test `tests/run/asyncgen_aclose_throw.pyx` throws into a pending `aclose()` while the generator awaits in its `finally` block:\r\n\r\n- master: `runtests.py asyncgen_aclose_throw` segfaults (exit 139)\r\n- this branch: the test passes\r\n- the same code passes as plain Python",
    "closed_at": null,
