            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Could we rename this file to `.py` rather than `.pyx`? That would mean the tests also run under plain Python which gives a bit of assurance that we're matching Python behaviour. I don't think this file uses any Cython-specific syntax so it should be compatible.\n\n(Obviously if there's any Python bugs here then we may need to exclude specific Python versions. The `pure3.x` tag does that (e.g. `pure3.11` to run on 3.11 or above). But deal with that if it happens)",
